package com.mazharansari.axion.ui.settings

/** v0.5.2: Privacy Policy, Security and Terms of Use — plain English, the same words as axion_privacy_policy.html. */
object PolicyText {
    const val UPDATED = "November 1, 2026 (v0.5.3)"
    data class Doc(val title: String, val sections: List<Pair<String, String>>)
    val privacy = Doc("Privacy Policy", listOf(
        "Short version" to "Axion is an app on your phone. There is no Axion server. Signing in is optional (you can continue as a guest). Your chats, keys and projects stay on this phone. When you send a message, it goes from your phone straight to the AI company you picked (for example Google Gemini or Groq), using your own key. The developer of Axion never sees your chats, keys, files or projects.",
        "Who we are" to "Axion is made by Mazhar Ansari. Contact: mazharalam4447@gmail.com. This policy applies to the Axion Android app.",
        "Sign-in" to "Sign-in (Google, email and password, or GitHub) is handled by Google Firebase Authentication. Axion uses only your account email, name and user ID (and your profile photo, shown in Settings → Account). Your chats and keys stay on this device and are never uploaded to Firebase. Signing in to Axion does not sign you in to Antigravity, and signing out or continuing as a guest does not delete anything on the phone.",
        "What is stored on your phone" to "• Your API keys, publishing tokens (Netlify, Vercel, Cloudflare, GitHub), MCP tokens and voice keys: encrypted with a key that lives in the Android Keystore and never leaves it.\n• Your Antigravity (Google) sign-ins: encrypted the same way. They are unlocked only while an Antigravity run needs them, then locked again.\n• Your chats and Build projects, files you upload and files Axion creates, your settings, and usage counters for the Quota screen. These stay in Axion's private storage, which other apps can't read. API keys are masked in saved chats.\n• Optional downloads you choose: the Linux system, developer tools, local AI models.",
        "What leaves your phone, and where it goes" to "Only what is needed for the feature you use, sent directly from your phone over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection:\n• Your messages, attached files and the recent chat → the AI provider you connected (Google Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, Cerebras, Mistral and others), with your key.\n• \"Free (slow)\" (only used when no key works) → Pollinations, with no key.\n• Build mode → Google Antigravity, through your Google account.\n• \"My server\" → your own server. \"Local model\" runs on the phone and sends nothing.\n• Web search and reading pages (when the AI uses them) → DuckDuckGo or Bing and the pages being read.\n• Voice: dictation uses your phone's speech recognizer; read-aloud uses Microsoft's Edge voices, Google Gemini or ElevenLabs (whichever you pick); voice calls use Google Gemini Live.\n• Publishing a website → Netlify, Vercel, Cloudflare or GitHub, with your token.\n• Downloads (Linux, tools, models) → Ubuntu, npm, Python, Hugging Face and similar public servers.\n• Sign-in (only if you sign in) → Google Firebase Authentication: your email, name and user ID. With GitHub sign-in, GitHub shares your public profile with Firebase.\n• Update check → claworabeauty.store, to read the latest version number and download the update. Nothing about you is sent.\nEach of these companies handles data under its own privacy policy. Axion never sells or shares your data with anyone else.",
        "What Axion does NOT do" to "• No Axion server receives your chats, keys, files or projects.\n• No ads, no analytics, no tracking, no crash-report service.\n• No Google Drive / cloud backup of Axion data, and no copying to a new phone by Android's transfer tool. Keys move only through \"Export / import keys\", in a file locked with your password.\n• Your key is only ever sent to the company that issued it.",
        "Permissions" to "Microphone (dictation and voice calls), camera (taking a photo to send), internet, notifications for downloads and updates, and \"install apps\" (only to install Axion updates and APKs you build). Each is used only when you use that feature.",
        "Children" to "Axion is not made for children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.",
        "Deleting your data" to "Settings → About → Delete all data erases everything Axion has stored on this phone: keys, tokens, sign-ins, chats, projects, files, Linux and models, and the Keystore key itself. Uninstalling Axion does the same. Files you saved to Downloads/Axion stay there because they are yours. To cancel a key or token completely, also delete it on the provider's website (for example Google AI Studio or Groq Console).",
        "Changes" to "If this policy changes, the new version will be in the app and at the same web address, with a new date.",
    ))
    val security = Doc("Security", listOf(
        "Your keys" to "• Encrypted on the phone with AES-256-GCM. The encryption key is created inside the Android Keystore (hardware-backed on most phones) and can't be copied out.\n• Never written to logs, notifications or crash reports, and never saved in plain text.\n• Shown masked, with only the last 4 characters.\n• Sent only to the company that issued the key, over HTTPS, in a request header (not in the web address).\n• Screens where you type or see a key block screenshots and screen recording.\n• Copied text that contains a key is hidden from the clipboard preview and cleared after 45 seconds.",
        "Connections" to "Axion only talks to the internet over HTTPS. Unencrypted http is blocked, except to the phone itself (the website preview). Certificates you installed yourself are not trusted, so they can't be used to read Axion's traffic.",
        "Backups" to "Axion's data is excluded from Google backup and phone-to-phone transfer, so your keys can't leak through a backup.",
        "Export file" to "\"Export / import keys\" makes a file locked with your password (AES-256-GCM, key made with PBKDF2 using 600,000 rounds and a random salt). Without the password the file can't be read, and a wrong password reveals nothing. Keep the file for yourself and never send it together with its password.",
        "Build agent, Linux and your projects" to "• Keys and tokens are never put into Linux, environment variables or project files. The AI and the code it writes can't read them.\n• Antigravity sign-ins are encrypted when no run is using them.\n• Anything that looks like a key is masked in command output, chat history and errors, and is never sent back to the AI.\n• Before publishing a website or building an APK, Axion scans the files. If a key is found, it stops and shows you where it is.\n• Sharing or saving a text file that contains a key is blocked until the key is removed.\n• The website preview can't open files on your phone and has no bridge into the app.",
        "Updates" to "An update is installed only if its checksum matches and it is signed with Axion's own signing key. Android also refuses an update from a different key.",
        "If something goes wrong" to "If you think a key leaked, delete it at the provider (Google AI Studio, Groq Console, GitHub settings…) and add a new one. To report a security problem, email mazharalam4447@gmail.com.",
    ))
    val terms = Doc("Terms of Use", listOf(
        "Using Axion" to "Axion is free. You use it with your own accounts and API keys. You are responsible for following the terms of each AI provider, Google Antigravity and publishing service you connect, including their usage limits.",
        "Your content" to "Your messages, files and projects belong to you. Axion claims no rights to them. Don't use Axion for anything illegal or to harm others.",
        "AI answers" to "AI can be wrong. Check important answers (health, money, legal) with a qualified person. Code and apps the AI builds should be reviewed before you rely on them or publish them.",
        "Third-party services" to "Answers, publishing and downloads come from other companies' services. Axion does not control them and is not responsible for their availability, limits, costs or content.",
        "No warranty" to "Axion is provided \"as is\", without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, the developer is not liable for any loss arising from the use of the app, including lost data or charges from third-party services.",
        "Changes and contact" to "These terms may be updated in a new version of the app. Questions: mazharalam4447@gmail.com.",
    ))
}
